leanne_sales: Aurora Systems kickoff tomorrow AM. They need a POC: streaming SDK, model-initiated synchronous webhook calls (model waits for webhook response), and strict JSON invoice schema enforcement at the edge. Also asking Hosted vs Dedicated pricing, SOC2 + customer KMS, and IP allowlist/VPC options. Can someone bring a minimal SDK snippet + a 1-page runbook?

marta_presales: I can cover the runbook. Quick clarifying q's: expected peak QPS and average tokens per output? Are tool calls frequently nested or single-shot?

leanne_sales: Peak ~60 QPS, avg ~95 tokens/response. Tool calls ~1/6 responses, single-shot (no nested calls). p50 <120ms p95 <320ms. SOC2 required; they insist on customer-managed KMS.

jamie_devrel: Minimal JS streaming pattern (pseudo):
```js
const rw = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, routing: 'dedicated' });
const s = rw.stream({ model: 'redwood-rtf-1', streaming: true, functions: [INVOICE_TOOL] });
s.on('data', chunk => process.stdout.write(chunk.text));
s.on('function_call', async (call) => {
  const res = await fetch(call.url, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(call.args), timeout: 2500 });
  const json = await res.json();
  s.resumeWithFunctionResult(json);
});
```
Edge should validate a top-level "invoice" object with fields: invoice_id (string), total_cents (number), currency (string), line_items: array of {desc:string, qty:number, unit_cents:number}. If validation fails, mark response as invalid and trigger a verification model or human review.

rory_sre: Infra notes: To hit p50 targets use Dedicated routing + small batch sizes (max_batch_size=6, max_wait_ms=10) and KV prefix caching. For sync webhook calls make sure your webhook endpoint responds <2s; we recommend timeouts ~2s and circuit-breaker to avoid request pile-up. IP allowlist + private CIDR access -> requires Private deployment or Dedicated with VPC peering & static egress. Customer KMS supported but needs key policy config and short onboarding window.

marta_presales: I'll draft the 1-pager runbook: checklist (env vars, routing mode, batching, cache hints, function spec), smoke tests (streaming + mock webhook + schema validator), perf test plan, and security mapping (SOC2 doc + KMS steps + VPC options). Will push to presales repo and link in the deal folder.

leanne_sales: Great. @jamie_devrel add a tiny pytest harness or node script we can run during the call to show streaming + sync call working. @rory_sre please drop the SOC2 attestation and KMS onboarding doc in the deal folder. I'll share the security questionnaire now so you can map requirements.

jamie_devrel: Will do a 2-file demo: (1) mock webhook server (express) that echoes invoice JSON, (2) client streaming script that resumes with function result and runs schema check. Keep it tiny so we can demo in 10 minutes.

rory_sre: Dropping SOC2 PDF and KMS checklist to the folder. Also note: Dedicated + burst-hosting is a solid pricing approach for this footprint; finance can give numbers but expect mid-five-figures/mo baseline for reserved capacity.

leanne_sales: Thanks team — scheduling 9:30am demo. I'll send Aurora the runbook and invite them to fill the security questionnaire before the call.
